# Week 1 review: habits under pressure
teaches: ["safety/three-questions","safety/threats","calculation/in-between-move","endgames/conversion"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach","b":"gemini:Puck | eager club player, relaxed and good-humoured; never exaggerated"}
prompt: "Can you use the three questions when nobody tells you which tactic is coming? Can you finish a won ending against the computer?"
next: {"title":"How can one move attack two things?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/chess-30-days/08-how-can-one-move-attack-two-things.cast"}

## Warm-up: checks first
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 4n1k1/pp3p1p/1b4p1/8/8/2N3P1/PP3PKP/3qR3 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxe8+, Kg7, Nxd1]}
      - {fen: 1r4k1/1P3ppp/8/8/8/8/q4PPP/2R3K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rc8+, Rxc8, bxc8=Q#]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title Warm-up

A: Week one, reviewed: can you use the Three Questions when nobody tells you what's coming? Two warm-ups first.
    draw position

B: Black just took my queen on d1. I take back, obviously.
    highlight piece_d1

A: Captures can wait one move. Ask the questions in order: checks first.
    highlight piece_g8

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first.","Your rook on e1."] themes ["in-between move"] voice a
        right: Rook takes e8, check. Only then does the knight take the queen: one move in between wins a whole piece.
        wrong: Before you take back, is there a check?

    animate plies_shown 1 duration 0.4

B: The queen wasn't going anywhere. I could take it a move later.
    animate plies_shown 3 duration 2.6

A: Second one. Your pawn on b7 wants to queen,
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: and the rook on b8 stands in the way.
    highlight piece_b8

B: Rook to c8 is check. But his rook just takes it.
    highlight piece_c1

A: Then it's your move again. Keep going.
    highlight piece_b7

    pause 0.3

    ask "Calculate to the end." widget chess line true hints ["Start with the check.","After the rook takes, what can the pawn take?"] themes ["deflection","back rank"] voice a teaches ["tactics/deflection","safety/back-rank"]
        right: Rook to c8, check; the rook has to take, and the pawn takes back and queens, with mate.
        wrong: Don't stop when he takes your rook: whose move is it then?

B: Mate. I'd have stopped at 'he just takes it'.
    point at.ref piece_g8 gesture circle

A: Checks first, and calculate to the end. You'll need both today.
    highlight piece_c8

## The habit under pressure
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 4r1k1/pp3ppp/8/2b1q3/8/1N6/PP1Q1PPP/2R3K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxc5, Qe1+, Qxe1, Rxe1#]}
      - {fen: 4r1k1/pp3ppp/8/2b1q3/8/1N6/PP1Q1PPP/2R3K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Nxc5]}
      - {fen: 8/8/8/4k3/8/8/8/R3K3 w - - 0 1, moves: [Ra5+, Kd4, Ra4+, Kc3, Ra3+, Kb4]}
      - {fen: 8/8/1k6/8/7R/2K5/8/8 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rh5, Kc6, Kb4, Kb6, Rh6+, Kb7], arrows: [{from: h4, to: a4}], highlights: [a5, b5, c5]}
      - {fen: 3k4/R7/3K4/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1, moves: [Ra8#]}
      - {fen: k7/1RK5/8/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "The habit under pressure"

A: Now the habit under pressure. White to move, and nobody says what's coming.
    draw position

B: Black's bishop is attacked twice and guarded once.
    highlight piece_c5

B: I take it with the rook.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Now ask the Three Questions for Black. Checks first.
    highlight piece_e5

A: Queen to e1, check.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.3

A: Your queen must take, and his rook takes back: mate.
    animate plies_shown 4 duration 2.4

B: My rook was guarding the back rank, and I took it away.
    point at.ref sq_c1 gesture circle

A: There's a safe way to win that bishop. Find it.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Two pieces attack the bishop. Which one is cheaper?","Your knight on b3."] themes ["counting"] voice a teaches ["calculation/counting"]
        right: Knight takes c5. If the queen takes back, the rook takes her, and the rook never leaves the back rank.
        wrong: Which of your two attackers can take without leaving your back rank?

A: So ask the questions twice: for your move, then for the reply it allows.
    highlight piece_c1

A: The week's other question: can you finish a won game?
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: A rook up, nothing else left.
    highlight piece_a1

B: Easy. I just keep checking him.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

A: Three checks,
    animate plies_shown 3 duration 2.4

A: and now his king attacks your rook.
    animate plies_shown 6 duration 3

A: Checks only push him around.
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: Cut him off instead: the rook on the fourth rank is a fence.
    draw arrow_0

A: His king lives above it, and the fence only ever moves one way: closer.
    highlight piece_b6

    erase arrow_0

A: So shrink the box: the fence moves up a rank.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.3

B: He steps aside, so I bring my king up, behind the fence.
    animate plies_shown 3 duration 2.4

A: Say he steps back in front of your king.
    animate plies_shown 4 duration 1.3

A: The kings face each other, and it's your move. What now?
    highlight piece_b4 piece_b6

    quiz "The kings face each other, and it's your move. What now?" on_canvas true voice a
        right: Check with the rook. Your king already covers a5, b5 and c5, so he must go back.
        wrong: If the rook leaves the fifth rank, which squares does your king still guard?
        + Check with the rook
        * Bring your king closer
        * Move the rook far away

    draw hl_a5 hl_b5 hl_c5 parallel true

A: Rook to h6, check, and back he goes. The box is a rank smaller.
    animate plies_shown 6 duration 2.4

    erase hl_a5 hl_b5 hl_c5

B: And again, until he's on the edge.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Finish it." widget chess line true hints ["The kings face each other.","Your rook to the back rank."] themes ["mating pattern"] voice a teaches ["tactics/mating-patterns"]
        right: Rook to a8, mate: your king covers the three squares in front of his.
        wrong: Which check can't he step away from?

A: One warning: if he has no move and he's not in check,
    animate position_shown 5 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: that's stalemate, a draw.
    point at.ref piece_a8 gesture circle

A: Fence, king up, check when the kings face each other. That's the whole method.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 1 duration 0.6

## Your turn: the week-one test
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: Five for five. Week one has stuck.
    good: Most of them. The misses are your training list.
    poor: A week is short. The misses come back until they stick.
    none: The test will wait for you.
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: r4rk1/pppn1pp1/7p/8/7q/2N5/PPP1QPPP/3R1RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxd7]}
      - {fen: r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 4 4, moves: [Qxf7#]}
      - {fen: r2Q1bk1/ppp2ppp/8/8/3n4/8/PPP1BPPP/1N3RK1 b - - 0 1, moves: [Nxe2+, Kh1, Rxd8], flip: true}
      - {fen: r2q1rk1/pp3ppp/8/8/1b6/1P6/PB3PPP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qg4, g6, Qxb4]}
      - {fen: 7k/5K2/8/8/8/8/8/6R1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rh1#]}
      - {fen: 8/8/4k3/8/R7/8/4K3/8 w - - 0 1}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "Your turn"

A: You've seen the habit hold under pressure. Now your turn: five positions, no labels, and a score at the end.
    draw position

A: First one. Black's queen has just left d8.
    highlight piece_h4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["What did the queen stop guarding?","Your rook on d1."] themes ["hanging piece"] voice a test week1 teaches ["safety/hanging-pieces"]
        right: Rook takes d7: the queen was the knight's only guard, and she left.
        wrong: Ask what Black's last move left behind.

A: Next, an opening. Black's last move was knight to f6.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first.","f7 is guarded only by the king."] themes ["opening","mating pattern"] voice a test week1 teaches ["openings/principles","tactics/mating-patterns"]
        right: Queen takes f7, mate. The knight attacked your queen, but a check comes first, and f7 was guarded only by the king.
        wrong: Look at every check, even one that captures.

A: Black to move now. White's queen has just taken on d8.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Checks before captures.","Your knight on d4."] themes ["in-between move"] voice a test week1
        right: Knight takes e2, check, and only then rook takes d8: a bishop for free.
        wrong: The queen on d8 can wait one move. Is there a check first?

A: Back to White. Nothing hangs yet.
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Look for a move that makes two threats.","Your bishop on b2 already aims at g7."] themes ["threat"] voice a test week1
        right: Queen to g4 threatens mate on g7 and the loose bishop on b4. Black can't meet both.
        wrong: No capture works yet. Which queen move makes two threats at once?

A: Last one: today's ending.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Your king already covers g7 and g8.","Check along the h-file."] themes ["mating pattern","stalemate"] voice a test week1 teaches ["tactics/mating-patterns","endgames/saving-lost-games"]
        right: Rook to h1, mate. Rook to g7 looks like closing in, but it leaves him no move and no check: stalemate.
        wrong: He is in the corner. Which check leaves him no square?

    hide position

A: You scored {week1.score} of {week1.total}.
    results test week1

B: And the ones I missed?
    text review "Review" x 500 y 400 font_size 64

A: They go on your list. Here they come back, with any you missed earlier this week.
    explore activity review_misses

    erase review

    show position

A: Now finish one against the computer.
    animate position_shown 5 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: King and rook: mate him within twenty moves.
    explore activity vs_computer goal.kind mate goal.within 20 store krk

    hide position

A: Under pressure the habit stays the same: checks, captures, threats,
    text q_checks "checks" x 500 y 470 font_size 56
    text q_captures "captures" x 500 y 385 font_size 56
    text q_threats "threats" x 500 y 300 font_size 56

A: for both sides, then calculate to the end.
    highlight q_checks q_captures q_threats

A: Homework: one slow game today, fifteen plus ten or slower. Then find its first mistake.
    text hw "15 + 10" x 500 y 190 font_size 44

## Where next
end_page: true

    text end_next_kicker "Next" x 500 y 540 font_size 26 style.opacity 0.6
    link end_next href lecture:8 title "How can one move attack two things?" form title size 600 x 500 y 420

    link end_again href lecture:7 title "Watch again" form text mark replay open here x 500 y 250 font_size 28
    text end_count "7 of 30" x 500 y 180 font_size 22 style.opacity 0.6
